direction: down

title: |md
  ## Single probe vs multi-probe attach
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

single: "Single attach (legacy)" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  s_body: |md
    For each of N functions to trace:
    1. perf_event_open() syscall
    2. allocate kernel kprobe object
    3. install int3 (or trampoline)
    4. one BPF link per attach

    **Costs:**
    - N syscalls (slow startup for N=1000+)
    - N tracepoint listeners
    - N file descriptors
    - O(N) attach latency
  |
}

multi: "Multi-probe attach (modern, since 5.18)" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  m_body: |md
    Single attach for N functions:
    1. **One** BPF_LINK_CREATE syscall
    2. Pass list of N functions/offsets
    3. Kernel installs all N probes in one go
    4. **One** BPF link covers all N

    **Costs:**
    - 1 syscall
    - 1 BPF link
    - O(N) install but no per-syscall overhead
    - 10-100× faster startup for large N
  |
}

api: "API:\nbpf_program__attach_kprobe_multi_opts(\n  prog, NULL, &opts);\n+ struct bpf_kprobe_multi_opts {\n   .syms = symbols_array,\n   .cnt = N,\n  };" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
}

single -> multi: "modern code\nshould use this" {style.stroke-dash: 4}
multi -> api {style.stroke-dash: 4}
